1
00:00:03,580 --> 00:00:05,840
You'll never believe what happened to me at work today.

2
00:00:05,840 --> 00:00:09,400
This old guy was choking on his food, and I saved his life.

3
00:00:09,400 --> 00:00:10,570
You're kidding. Did you Heimlich him?

4
00:00:10,570 --> 00:00:13,030
No. I said, "Oh, my God, I think that old guy's choking,"

5
00:00:13,030 --> 00:00:15,220
and then one of the busboys Heimlich'ed him.

6
00:00:17,530 --> 00:00:18,960
You're a hero.

7
00:00:19,620 --> 00:00:22,090
Yeah, that was the point of the story.

8
00:00:23,670 --> 00:00:24,960
Oh, yeah, speaking of work, do you know

9
00:00:24,960 --> 00:00:26,260
if you have Thursday night off?

10
00:00:26,260 --> 00:00:28,090
Um, I think so. Why?

11
00:00:28,090 --> 00:00:29,790
What do you mean, why? It's Valentine's Day.

12
00:00:29,790 --> 00:00:30,890
Oh, right.

13
00:00:30,900 --> 00:00:32,550
Yeah, we can do something.

14
00:00:33,520 --> 00:00:34,860
You could be a little more into it.

15
00:00:34,860 --> 00:00:36,560
No, I'm into it, I'm into it.

16
00:00:36,560 --> 00:00:38,620
Just, there's so much pressure to make the night special,

17
00:00:38,620 --> 00:00:40,220
and it never works out.

18
00:00:40,220 --> 00:00:42,150
Okay, well, this time it's going to be different.

19
00:00:42,150 --> 00:00:45,050
Because I am like a romance ninja.

20
00:00:46,180 --> 00:00:47,640
You don't see it coming, and then bam!

21
00:00:47,640 --> 00:00:50,930
Romance, watch out, hearts, kisses, love, ooh-ya!

22
00:00:52,600 --> 00:00:53,910
You know, sometimes I think I've made you

23
00:00:53,910 --> 00:00:55,300
so much cooler than you used to be,

24
00:00:55,300 --> 00:00:57,160
and then you go and do that.

25
00:00:59,360 --> 00:01:00,750
So, in conclusion,

26
00:01:00,750 --> 00:01:03,480
I believe the painful sensation felt

27
00:01:03,480 --> 00:01:05,920
after passing a meal of spicy chilies

28
00:01:05,920 --> 00:01:10,440
is proof that the rectum does possess the sense of taste.

29
00:01:15,720 --> 00:01:17,660
I concur, but you changed the subject.

30
00:01:17,660 --> 00:01:20,000
What are we doing for Valentine's Day?

31
00:01:20,820 --> 00:01:22,850
Oh, you caught that, did you?

32
00:01:51,520 --> 00:01:52,990
Okay.

33
00:01:53,580 --> 00:01:55,000
Okay.

34
00:01:56,500 --> 00:01:57,930
Okay.

35
00:01:59,100 --> 00:02:00,540
Okay.

36
00:02:00,690 --> 00:02:02,400
Okay!

37
00:02:05,950 --> 00:02:07,340
Okay.

38
00:02:09,830 --> 00:02:11,440
Everything okay?

39
00:02:15,220 --> 00:02:16,340
Bernie's a little cranky

40
00:02:16,340 --> 00:02:18,820
since she's been working, like, 17 hours a day.

41
00:02:18,820 --> 00:02:20,490
And I've got a lot on my plate, too, because I've been

42
00:02:20,490 --> 00:02:23,080
busting my tail playing Assassin's Creed.

43
00:02:24,120 --> 00:02:24,780
Hey, Stuart,

44
00:02:24,790 --> 00:02:26,810
you got anything going on for Valentine's Day?

45
00:02:26,820 --> 00:02:27,530
Not really.

46
00:02:27,530 --> 00:02:30,260
Other than hiding all the sharp objects around here

47
00:02:30,260 --> 00:02:33,110
and white-knuckling it till morning.

48
00:02:33,190 --> 00:02:34,760
What do you got going on?

49
00:02:34,760 --> 00:02:36,300
Oh, well, I was going to spend the night

50
00:02:36,300 --> 00:02:38,430
with my special little lady, but, uh,

51
00:02:38,430 --> 00:02:41,230
she got worms, and then I had to take her to the vet.

52
00:02:45,030 --> 00:02:46,700
There must be something we can do.

53
00:02:46,700 --> 00:02:49,780
Well, uh, how about you keep the store open late,

54
00:02:49,780 --> 00:02:51,530
and we throw a party for all the people

55
00:02:51,530 --> 00:02:53,100
who don't have dates?

56
00:02:53,100 --> 00:02:55,210
That actually sounds kind of nice.

57
00:02:55,210 --> 00:02:56,740
Yeah, the theme will be that the greatest love

58
00:02:56,740 --> 00:03:00,120
a man can have is the love he has with himself.

59
00:03:03,030 --> 00:03:04,270
That's good.

60
00:03:04,280 --> 00:03:08,420
Or maybe something a little less "Hand in the pants."

61
00:03:11,050 --> 00:03:12,440
Oh, Alex, excellent.

62
00:03:12,440 --> 00:03:14,850
I have a research problem

63
00:03:14,850 --> 00:03:16,760
that I believe you can help with.

64
00:03:16,760 --> 00:03:18,780
Oh, Dr. Cooper, thank you.

65
00:03:18,780 --> 00:03:20,300
I've been waiting for an opportunity

66
00:03:20,300 --> 00:03:22,780
to contribute to your scientific work.

67
00:03:22,780 --> 00:03:26,170
Oh, no, no. That's not going to happen, no.

68
00:03:26,790 --> 00:03:31,050
What I need you to do is find a Valentine's gift

69
00:03:31,050 --> 00:03:33,010
for my girlfriend.

70
00:03:33,880 --> 00:03:35,780
You realize I passed up an opportunity

71
00:03:35,780 --> 00:03:38,920
to work at Fermilab to take this job with you.

72
00:03:39,170 --> 00:03:41,900
Well, I guess those chaps will have to have

73
00:03:41,900 --> 00:03:43,540
someone else buy their girlfriends presents.

74
00:03:43,550 --> 00:03:46,530
Now, here is...

75
00:03:46,540 --> 00:03:48,000
Let's see.

76
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:50,230
This is...

77
00:03:53,230 --> 00:03:55,970
This is about $2,000.

78
00:03:56,330 --> 00:04:00,880
Um, I think she likes monkeys and the color gray.

79
00:04:07,080 --> 00:04:09,530
Contribute to my work.

80
00:04:11,930 --> 00:04:15,200
Ah, kids say the darnedest things.

81
00:04:17,510 --> 00:04:18,600
Hey, you coming to lunch?

82
00:04:18,600 --> 00:04:19,800
Yeah, one second.

83
00:04:19,800 --> 00:04:21,040
Come here. I want to show you something.

84
00:04:21,040 --> 00:04:21,790
What you looking at?

85
00:04:21,790 --> 00:04:23,920
Well, I was trying to come up with something

86
00:04:23,920 --> 00:04:26,580
really romantic to give Bernadette

87
00:04:26,580 --> 00:04:28,250
for Valentine's Day since she's been

88
00:04:28,250 --> 00:04:30,710
such a pain in the ass.

89
00:04:33,040 --> 00:04:35,280
You can't find a card that says that?

90
00:04:36,720 --> 00:04:37,220
Check it out.

91
00:04:37,220 --> 00:04:38,750
I used the atomic force microscope

92
00:04:38,750 --> 00:04:42,280
in the material science lab and wrote our initials

93
00:04:42,290 --> 00:04:45,930
in a heart 1/1,000 the size of a grain of sand.

94
00:04:46,600 --> 00:04:48,780
Oh, that's cool.

95
00:04:48,790 --> 00:04:52,920
A micro-valentine for a microbiologist.

96
00:04:53,610 --> 00:04:55,760
From her micro-husband.

97
00:04:59,970 --> 00:05:01,060
That is amazing.

98
00:05:01,060 --> 00:05:02,390
How long did this take you?

99
00:05:02,390 --> 00:05:04,660
Mmm, about 12 hours.

100
00:05:04,660 --> 00:05:06,650
I pulled an all-nighter.

101
00:05:06,950 --> 00:05:08,770
Yeah, I know, it really took a bite

102
00:05:08,770 --> 00:05:11,010
out of my video game time.

103
00:05:11,690 --> 00:05:13,030
What are you and Penny doing?

104
00:05:13,030 --> 00:05:16,280
Oh, I'm going to take her to a nice restaurant for dinner.

105
00:05:16,280 --> 00:05:19,380
Oh, that's not bad, but as far as romance goes,

106
00:05:19,380 --> 00:05:22,210
I think my gift hits it right out of...

107
00:05:26,340 --> 00:05:28,680
- Want to come to dinner with us? - Yes, please.

108
00:05:31,030 --> 00:05:32,210
Okay.

109
00:05:32,210 --> 00:05:34,150
Amy will be here shortly,

110
00:05:34,150 --> 00:05:37,720
expecting the perfect Valentine's gift, so...

111
00:05:37,720 --> 00:05:38,680
you're up kid.

112
00:05:38,680 --> 00:05:40,380
Dazzle me. Go.

113
00:05:41,630 --> 00:05:44,030
Okay, I think I have some really great choices.

114
00:05:44,030 --> 00:05:45,450
I went on Amy's Facebook page

115
00:05:45,450 --> 00:05:46,700
and read up on her interests.

116
00:05:46,700 --> 00:05:50,740
Now, see, I never would have thought to do that.

117
00:05:51,180 --> 00:05:52,640
Clearly, I made a good choice

118
00:05:52,640 --> 00:05:53,750
farming this out to you.

119
00:05:53,760 --> 00:05:54,320
But I am telling you,

120
00:05:54,320 --> 00:05:56,360
Amy hit the boyfriend jackpot.

121
00:05:56,360 --> 00:05:59,610
Anyway, my socks are on.

122
00:05:59,610 --> 00:06:01,530
Let's knock them off.

123
00:06:05,570 --> 00:06:08,550
Well, um, I know she loves playing the harp,

124
00:06:08,550 --> 00:06:12,840
so I found this beautiful music box

125
00:06:12,840 --> 00:06:15,600
that plays one of her favorite songs.

126
00:06:17,590 --> 00:06:20,330
Now, Amy already has a real harp.

127
00:06:20,970 --> 00:06:22,970
And it can play any song.

128
00:06:24,430 --> 00:06:26,180
What are you trying to pull here?

129
00:06:27,610 --> 00:06:30,170
- No, I just thought it would be... - Next.

130
00:06:31,690 --> 00:06:32,920
Okay.

131
00:06:32,920 --> 00:06:34,930
Um, I know she's a fan of The Canterbury Tales,

132
00:06:34,930 --> 00:06:38,150
so I found...

133
00:06:38,420 --> 00:06:40,120
this cool map

134
00:06:40,120 --> 00:06:42,410
that illustrates the characters' journey through England.

135
00:06:42,420 --> 00:06:44,910
I thought we could put it in a really nice frame.

136
00:06:45,610 --> 00:06:48,890
But she's got Google Maps on her phone.

137
00:06:52,330 --> 00:06:54,290
I don't know how to respond to that.

138
00:06:55,730 --> 00:06:57,870
Well, I hope it's with a third good option,

139
00:06:57,870 --> 00:07:00,790
because these first two... blah.

140
00:07:03,160 --> 00:07:04,070
Okay.

141
00:07:04,070 --> 00:07:07,560
Well, uh, luckily, I saved the best for last.

142
00:07:07,560 --> 00:07:09,150
Since Amy's a neuroscientist,

143
00:07:09,150 --> 00:07:10,960
I did some research and found out

144
00:07:10,960 --> 00:07:12,720
that Santiago Ramony Cajal,

145
00:07:12,720 --> 00:07:14,800
the father of modern neuroscience,

146
00:07:14,800 --> 00:07:17,710
did lots of hand drawings of brain cells.

147
00:07:17,710 --> 00:07:20,320
And I managed to find

148
00:07:20,320 --> 00:07:23,640
this signed print.

149
00:07:25,620 --> 00:07:28,400
Oh, this is truly remarkable.

150
00:07:28,400 --> 00:07:29,400
Thank you.

151
00:07:29,400 --> 00:07:31,760
I think I'll keep it for myself.

152
00:07:35,200 --> 00:07:36,250
What about your girlfriend?

153
00:07:36,250 --> 00:07:38,450
It's too late. I call dibs.

154
00:07:43,120 --> 00:07:44,760
This place is really beautiful.

155
00:07:44,760 --> 00:07:47,620
Wah... romance ninja.

156
00:07:51,250 --> 00:07:52,880
Sorry we're late.

157
00:07:52,880 --> 00:07:54,330
No problem. We just sat down.

158
00:07:54,330 --> 00:07:55,910
Mmm, would you like some wine?

159
00:07:55,910 --> 00:07:57,670
Yeah, fill her up.

160
00:07:59,860 --> 00:08:01,980
I'll tell you when to stop.

161
00:08:03,960 --> 00:08:05,230
Is everything okay?

162
00:08:05,230 --> 00:08:07,250
Terrific. Couldn't be better.

163
00:08:07,250 --> 00:08:09,150
Oh, bite me.

164
00:08:10,650 --> 00:08:12,230
Look, we can still have a nice night.

165
00:08:12,240 --> 00:08:13,420
Just tell me where it is.

166
00:08:13,420 --> 00:08:16,690
Maybe if you did what you said you were going to do, I'd tell you.

167
00:08:16,690 --> 00:08:18,270
Uh, where what is?

168
00:08:18,270 --> 00:08:20,820
She hid my XBOX like I'm a child.

169
00:08:22,610 --> 00:08:24,110
Yeah, and my mom got me that for my birthday,

170
00:08:24,110 --> 00:08:26,280
so if you don't give it back, I'm telling.

171
00:08:28,350 --> 00:08:30,110
I've been working late every night.

172
00:08:30,110 --> 00:08:31,040
All I asked was that he

173
00:08:31,040 --> 00:08:33,010
clean the apartment and do one load of laundry.

174
00:08:33,010 --> 00:08:34,050
But did he do it? No.

175
00:08:34,050 --> 00:08:36,220
He just kept on playing that stupid game.

176
00:08:36,220 --> 00:08:37,540
You like pushing buttons so much,

177
00:08:37,540 --> 00:08:39,910
try pushing them on the washing machine.

178
00:08:41,840 --> 00:08:43,310
I said I'm sorry.

179
00:08:43,310 --> 00:08:45,960
Sorry doesn't clean my underpants, buddy.

180
00:08:47,350 --> 00:08:50,460
I told you, turn them inside out.

181
00:08:50,680 --> 00:08:53,340
And I told you to bite me.

182
00:08:54,760 --> 00:08:57,330
Trying to have a magical night here, guys.

183
00:09:01,310 --> 00:09:03,810
- Oh, son of a bitch. - What?

184
00:09:04,220 --> 00:09:05,550
Nothing. Nothing.

185
00:09:05,550 --> 00:09:06,920
No, tell me.

186
00:09:06,920 --> 00:09:09,460
It's just this guy I used to date.

187
00:09:10,810 --> 00:09:12,780
Until he cheated on me with my friend Gretchen,

188
00:09:12,780 --> 00:09:14,850
who's here with him now.

189
00:09:14,850 --> 00:09:16,290
You're kidding.

190
00:09:16,290 --> 00:09:19,150
And it looks like she lost a lot of weight, damn it.

191
00:09:20,830 --> 00:09:22,260
I know it's not ideal,

192
00:09:22,260 --> 00:09:23,810
but don't let them ruin our night.

193
00:09:23,820 --> 00:09:24,620
No, you're totally right.

194
00:09:24,620 --> 00:09:26,760
She could be skinny 'cause she's dying.

195
00:09:28,050 --> 00:09:29,810
That's the spirit.

196
00:09:30,180 --> 00:09:31,130
You know what, screw them.

197
00:09:31,130 --> 00:09:33,450
Our night is going to be way more special than theirs.

198
00:09:33,450 --> 00:09:34,890
Yeah.

199
00:09:39,530 --> 00:09:40,960
What?

200
00:09:41,230 --> 00:09:43,280
Oh, you got to be kidding me.

201
00:09:43,650 --> 00:09:45,350
Oh, my God, yes.

202
00:09:45,350 --> 00:09:47,340
Of course I'll marry you.

203
00:09:49,470 --> 00:09:50,920
Two can play this game.

204
00:09:50,920 --> 00:09:51,670
- Penny... - Get up.

205
00:09:51,670 --> 00:09:53,040
All right.

206
00:10:01,930 --> 00:10:04,840
It's nice that all the people who are lonely on Valentine's Day

207
00:10:04,840 --> 00:10:06,800
can come here tonight and be together.

208
00:10:06,800 --> 00:10:09,590
Yeah, I'm really looking forward to it.

209
00:10:09,590 --> 00:10:12,320
In fact, there's no place I would rather be than here.

210
00:10:12,330 --> 00:10:13,920
Except on a date with anybody.

211
00:10:13,920 --> 00:10:15,720
Literally anybody.

212
00:10:17,280 --> 00:10:19,670
You know, you and I have so much fun hanging out.

213
00:10:19,680 --> 00:10:20,570
If you were a girl,

214
00:10:20,570 --> 00:10:22,590
all our problems would be solved.

215
00:10:26,390 --> 00:10:27,700
What?

216
00:10:27,700 --> 00:10:28,790
Oh, yeah, think about it.

217
00:10:28,800 --> 00:10:30,260
We'd hang out,

218
00:10:30,260 --> 00:10:32,660
we'd read comic books, we'd see movies.

219
00:10:32,660 --> 00:10:35,590
It'd be like the best relationship ever.

220
00:10:35,590 --> 00:10:37,080
That does sound nice.

221
00:10:37,080 --> 00:10:39,760
Then I'd take you home, slip off your little black dress

222
00:10:39,760 --> 00:10:42,840
and just pile-drive you into oblivion.

223
00:10:45,850 --> 00:10:47,210
What?

224
00:10:49,710 --> 00:10:50,930
Oh, I can't believe

225
00:10:50,930 --> 00:10:53,410
he's going to marry the girl he cheated on me with.

226
00:10:53,410 --> 00:10:54,750
Isn't it kind of nice?

227
00:10:54,750 --> 00:10:56,150
I mean, he was with the wrong person,

228
00:10:56,150 --> 00:10:57,530
and now he found the right person.

229
00:10:57,530 --> 00:10:59,120
What, so I'm the wrong person?

230
00:10:59,130 --> 00:11:01,880
Maybe you want to be with Gretchen, too.

231
00:11:03,720 --> 00:11:05,180
They do look happy.

232
00:11:05,180 --> 00:11:06,360
Yeah, maybe tonight.

233
00:11:06,360 --> 00:11:07,350
But a year from now, he'll be

234
00:11:07,350 --> 00:11:10,090
crawling under the sink looking for his Xbox.

235
00:11:11,520 --> 00:11:13,050
Well, he will.

236
00:11:14,540 --> 00:11:16,200
You know what? Why don't we just forget about them

237
00:11:16,200 --> 00:11:18,140
and enjoy our Valentine's Day?

238
00:11:18,140 --> 00:11:20,380
Yes, absolutely.

239
00:11:25,450 --> 00:11:26,750
Now they're doing that phony

240
00:11:26,760 --> 00:11:29,120
link-arm-drink thingy.

241
00:11:29,340 --> 00:11:31,340
I totally taught him that.

242
00:11:33,600 --> 00:11:34,850
I thought we were letting it go.

243
00:11:34,860 --> 00:11:37,000
We were; it's just... it's not fair, okay?

244
00:11:37,000 --> 00:11:38,280
They're bad people.

245
00:11:38,280 --> 00:11:39,610
It's not supposed to end happy for them;

246
00:11:39,610 --> 00:11:41,740
it's supposed to end happy for me.

247
00:11:42,850 --> 00:11:44,430
It did end happy for you.

248
00:11:44,430 --> 00:11:45,300
You're here with me.

249
00:11:45,310 --> 00:11:47,010
Yeah, yeah, I know.

250
00:11:48,190 --> 00:11:50,170
Okay, this is getting a little hard to not take personally.

251
00:11:50,170 --> 00:11:51,630
Oh, come on, don't make this about you.

252
00:11:51,640 --> 00:11:53,390
Oh, I'm not. It's about you.

253
00:11:53,390 --> 00:11:54,560
Yeah, well, whatever, okay?

254
00:11:54,570 --> 00:11:56,190
I told you, Valentine's Day sucks.

255
00:11:56,190 --> 00:11:58,550
This one does, and you're the reason why.

256
00:11:58,550 --> 00:11:59,890
What?

257
00:12:00,880 --> 00:12:01,800
You know, compared to them,

258
00:12:01,810 --> 00:12:03,780
I'm feeling pretty good about us.

259
00:12:03,780 --> 00:12:04,720
Me, too.

260
00:12:04,720 --> 00:12:07,570
How about we blow off dessert, go home early...

261
00:12:07,570 --> 00:12:08,960
I'll do that laundry.

262
00:12:08,970 --> 00:12:10,230
Thank you.

263
00:12:10,230 --> 00:12:11,080
I love you.

264
00:12:11,080 --> 00:12:12,620
Love you, too.

265
00:12:14,190 --> 00:12:15,490
So where'd you hide it?

266
00:12:15,490 --> 00:12:17,620
Where you'd never look.

267
00:12:17,760 --> 00:12:20,420
Damn it, it's in the washing machine.

268
00:12:27,420 --> 00:12:28,670
Hello.

269
00:12:28,670 --> 00:12:30,030
Hello.

270
00:12:30,370 --> 00:12:31,680
Happy Valentine's Day.

271
00:12:31,680 --> 00:12:33,070
Okay.

272
00:12:36,130 --> 00:12:37,610
Shall we go to dinner?

273
00:12:37,610 --> 00:12:38,740
Hang on.

274
00:12:38,740 --> 00:12:41,320
As you know, I had planned a traditional evening

275
00:12:41,320 --> 00:12:43,240
of romance and gifts.

276
00:12:43,240 --> 00:12:43,950
Yes,

277
00:12:43,950 --> 00:12:45,090
and as you know,

278
00:12:45,090 --> 00:12:47,680
I planned to pretend to enjoy it.

279
00:12:48,590 --> 00:12:51,560
I've been working on this facial expression all day.

280
00:12:54,600 --> 00:12:56,410
And I appreciate your effort,

281
00:12:56,410 --> 00:12:57,930
but upon contemplation,

282
00:12:57,930 --> 00:13:00,170
I decided I was being selfish.

283
00:13:00,180 --> 00:13:02,350
So, I canceled our dinner reservations

284
00:13:02,350 --> 00:13:03,860
and came up with an even better way

285
00:13:03,860 --> 00:13:06,100
to celebrate Valentine's Day.

286
00:13:06,280 --> 00:13:07,300
What is that?

287
00:13:07,300 --> 00:13:08,960
By doing none of it--

288
00:13:08,960 --> 00:13:09,810
no dinner,

289
00:13:09,810 --> 00:13:11,760
no romance, no gifts.

290
00:13:11,760 --> 00:13:14,340
We stay here, order a pizza

291
00:13:14,340 --> 00:13:16,070
and watch one of your beloved

292
00:13:16,070 --> 00:13:18,380
Star War Trek things.

293
00:13:19,620 --> 00:13:21,140
Really?

294
00:13:21,230 --> 00:13:23,390
Well, that's what you'd love, isn't it?

295
00:13:23,390 --> 00:13:25,000
More than anything.

296
00:13:25,000 --> 00:13:26,390
Well, then...

297
00:13:26,560 --> 00:13:28,280
that's what we're going to do.

298
00:13:30,510 --> 00:13:33,890
Well... I don't know what to say.

299
00:13:34,220 --> 00:13:36,410
This is the most thoughtful gift

300
00:13:36,410 --> 00:13:38,430
that anyone's ever given me.

301
00:13:38,430 --> 00:13:40,170
And that's including an amazing gift

302
00:13:40,170 --> 00:13:42,470
that I gave myself earlier today.

303
00:13:44,620 --> 00:13:46,840
I'm your girlfriend. That's my job.

304
00:13:46,840 --> 00:13:50,070
And I know gift-giving puts a lot of pressure on you,

305
00:13:50,070 --> 00:13:54,010
so whatever you got me, you can return.

306
00:13:55,190 --> 00:13:56,500
No.

307
00:13:57,120 --> 00:13:59,480
No, after everything you didn't do for me tonight,

308
00:13:59,480 --> 00:14:01,240
I want you to have it.

309
00:14:02,220 --> 00:14:03,040
What's this?

310
00:14:03,040 --> 00:14:04,370
Read it.

311
00:14:05,120 --> 00:14:06,020
"Sheldon Cooper,

312
00:14:06,020 --> 00:14:08,690
Caltech University employee information"?

313
00:14:08,690 --> 00:14:10,160
At the bottom.

314
00:14:10,170 --> 00:14:13,290
"In case of emergency, please contact...

315
00:14:13,670 --> 00:14:15,770
Amy Farrah Fowler."

316
00:14:18,330 --> 00:14:20,490
And there's my phone number.

317
00:14:23,660 --> 00:14:26,950
This is the most beautiful gift you could've ever given me.

318
00:14:27,850 --> 00:14:28,900
Well, I thought,

319
00:14:28,900 --> 00:14:32,680
if I have a stroke or a kidney stone,

320
00:14:32,960 --> 00:14:35,270
who would I want to share that with?

321
00:14:38,880 --> 00:14:40,730
And you picked me.

322
00:14:42,030 --> 00:14:43,280
It's like you said--

323
00:14:43,280 --> 00:14:45,150
you're my girlfriend.

324
00:14:45,150 --> 00:14:47,500
Oh, Sheldon.

325
00:14:50,860 --> 00:14:52,440
Okay.

326
00:14:53,090 --> 00:14:56,180
Stop ruining Valentine's Day and order my pizza.

327
00:15:01,120 --> 00:15:03,050
- Night. - Yep.

328
00:15:12,380 --> 00:15:13,790
You know what?

329
00:15:13,960 --> 00:15:15,280
That was pretty crappy of you.

330
00:15:15,290 --> 00:15:17,880
I mean, all I wanted to do was give you a great night,

331
00:15:17,880 --> 00:15:20,630
and it's like you-you went out of your way to destroy it.

332
00:15:20,630 --> 00:15:21,770
Yeah, I know.

333
00:15:21,770 --> 00:15:22,740
I'm a total bitch.

334
00:15:22,750 --> 00:15:24,530
- I'm not saying that. - Well, I am.

335
00:15:24,530 --> 00:15:26,690
Fine, you win. You're a bitch.

336
00:15:29,110 --> 00:15:31,930
Why couldn't we just have a nice time?

337
00:15:31,930 --> 00:15:33,550
I don't know.

338
00:15:33,970 --> 00:15:36,640
Maybe 'cause things are going so well between us lately

339
00:15:36,640 --> 00:15:38,880
and I've been really happy.

340
00:15:45,170 --> 00:15:48,200
Okay, you're gonna have to make a lot more sense than that.

341
00:15:48,790 --> 00:15:51,780
Obviously, I have some commitment issues.

342
00:15:51,780 --> 00:15:53,720
Glaringly obvious. Go on.

343
00:15:54,290 --> 00:15:56,250
As long as things keep going great between us,

344
00:15:56,260 --> 00:15:57,640
you'll keep asking me to marry you,

345
00:15:57,640 --> 00:15:59,240
and eventually I'm gonna end up saying yes,

346
00:15:59,240 --> 00:16:00,910
and then we're gonna be married forever,

347
00:16:00,910 --> 00:16:03,830
and the whole thing just freaks me out.

348
00:16:05,580 --> 00:16:07,100
Okay.

349
00:16:07,930 --> 00:16:10,510
I know I propose a lot.

350
00:16:14,500 --> 00:16:16,840
So how about this?

351
00:16:17,790 --> 00:16:21,430
I promise I will never ask you to marry me again.

352
00:16:21,930 --> 00:16:23,410
What... what do you mean?

353
00:16:23,410 --> 00:16:24,650
Are you breaking up with me?

354
00:16:24,650 --> 00:16:25,420
No.

355
00:16:25,430 --> 00:16:26,330
No, no, no, no.

356
00:16:26,330 --> 00:16:29,700
But if someday you decide you want to get married,

357
00:16:29,700 --> 00:16:31,650
you have to propose to me.

358
00:16:32,300 --> 00:16:34,220
- Really? - Yes.

359
00:16:34,230 --> 00:16:35,950
It's all on you.

360
00:16:36,310 --> 00:16:37,980
But I got to tell you, when the time comes,

361
00:16:37,980 --> 00:16:38,910
I want the whole nine yards.

362
00:16:38,910 --> 00:16:40,190
I want you down on one knee, flowers.

363
00:16:40,200 --> 00:16:42,560
I want to be swept off my feet.

364
00:16:45,090 --> 00:16:46,390
Yeah, you got it.

365
00:16:46,400 --> 00:16:47,400
And I'm cool with surprises.

366
00:16:47,400 --> 00:16:49,450
But nothing on a Jumbotron.

367
00:16:50,910 --> 00:16:53,330
I don't want to cry on a big screen like that.

368
00:16:55,690 --> 00:16:56,970
Okay.

369
00:16:59,020 --> 00:17:00,450
You know what?

370
00:17:00,940 --> 00:17:02,330
This might be the wine talking,

371
00:17:02,330 --> 00:17:06,380
but I have a very important question to ask you.

372
00:17:07,150 --> 00:17:08,440
You do?

373
00:17:09,130 --> 00:17:11,080
Leonard Hofstadter...

374
00:17:11,770 --> 00:17:13,390
Yes?

375
00:17:15,290 --> 00:17:17,500
...will you be my valentine?

376
00:17:19,740 --> 00:17:21,570
Sorry. Maybe next year.

377
00:17:24,340 --> 00:17:25,140
I'm just kidding!

378
00:17:25,140 --> 00:17:27,610
Romance ninja. Let's have sex!

379
00:17:32,310 --> 00:17:34,060
Thank you, guys, for doing this.

380
00:17:34,060 --> 00:17:35,800
We're glad you could make it.

381
00:17:35,800 --> 00:17:38,810
Usually I spend Valentine's Day sad and alone.

382
00:17:38,810 --> 00:17:40,720
This year, I'm just sad.

383
00:17:43,440 --> 00:17:45,800
What is it about this holiday that makes people so unhappy?

384
00:17:45,810 --> 00:17:46,750
I know.

385
00:17:46,750 --> 00:17:48,390
I hate myself most of the time,

386
00:17:48,390 --> 00:17:51,800
but tonight's the night I know everyone else does, too.

387
00:17:52,880 --> 00:17:54,730
I think you're cool.

388
00:17:55,630 --> 00:17:57,040
Great.

389
00:17:59,620 --> 00:18:00,820
I got to tell you,

390
00:18:00,820 --> 00:18:03,720
we've got to stop beating ourselves up like this.

391
00:18:05,340 --> 00:18:07,150
Excuse me, everybody.

392
00:18:07,360 --> 00:18:09,430
Can I have your attention, please?

393
00:18:13,730 --> 00:18:16,030
We're all here tonight because...

394
00:18:16,030 --> 00:18:18,070
we have no one to be with.

395
00:18:18,520 --> 00:18:22,960
But... that doesn't make us mutants.

396
00:18:23,310 --> 00:18:26,670
The only mutants here are in these comic books.

397
00:18:28,290 --> 00:18:31,520
We've got to stop defining our self-worth

398
00:18:31,520 --> 00:18:34,550
by whether or not we're in a relationship.

399
00:18:35,410 --> 00:18:37,360
You know what I see when I look around?

400
00:18:38,490 --> 00:18:40,570
I see a room full of great people.

401
00:18:41,990 --> 00:18:44,710
So let's give ourselves a break.

402
00:18:44,710 --> 00:18:47,180
We are a community,

403
00:18:47,180 --> 00:18:49,650
and as long as we have each other,

404
00:18:49,720 --> 00:18:51,800
we're never truly alone.

405
00:18:59,440 --> 00:19:00,590
That was cool.

406
00:19:00,590 --> 00:19:02,060
What you said.

407
00:19:03,440 --> 00:19:04,660
You really think so?

408
00:19:04,670 --> 00:19:05,910
Yeah, I do.

409
00:19:05,920 --> 00:19:07,230
Thank you.

410
00:19:11,480 --> 00:19:12,980
Would you like to, uh...

411
00:19:12,980 --> 00:19:16,210
get a cup... A cup of coffee or...?

412
00:19:16,440 --> 00:19:17,860
Okay.

413
00:19:23,150 --> 00:19:25,190
Later, losers!

414
00:19:38,590 --> 00:19:40,090
Hello?

415
00:19:40,690 --> 00:19:42,200
Another medical emergency?

416
00:19:42,200 --> 00:19:44,040
What's wrong with him now?

417
00:19:45,600 --> 00:19:49,430
I seriously doubt he was bitten by a Chinese bird spider.

418
00:19:50,870 --> 00:19:53,760
How exactly does a bump feel Asian?

419
00:19:54,920 --> 00:19:56,570
Just put him on the phone.

420
00:19:57,090 --> 00:19:59,950
Sheldon, I am not driving over there again.

421
00:20:00,260 --> 00:20:01,720
Because I drove over there yesterday

422
00:20:01,720 --> 00:20:03,210
for a brain tumor that turned out to be

423
00:20:03,220 --> 00:20:04,960
an ice cream headache.

424
00:20:07,120 --> 00:20:10,810
Yes, I still want to be your emergency contact.

425
00:20:12,170 --> 00:20:14,710
Yes, you can eat your ice cream too fast

426
00:20:14,710 --> 00:20:16,960
and also have a brain tumor.

427
00:20:20,250 --> 00:20:21,680
I'm on my way.

428
00:20:24,520 --> 00:20:26,610
Brain tumor would explain a lot.

